 # Weather research and Kalshi on Cold Red Gate
 
+Same-day daily-rain research now retains compressed exact NWS observation response pages, validated accumulation quantities and raw METAR precipitation remarks. Trace, missing, conflicting and boundary-crossing measurements remain separate; overlapping windows are never added. Fully future NBH P01 marginals expose union bounds and an explicitly hypothetical independence value; partially elapsed hours and unobserved past rain prevent identification of the whole-day event. A supported measurable proxy witness supplies two forward experimental probabilities (0.99 and 0.95), each with a fixed, untrained NWS-to-final-TWC failure assumption. These supplement the frozen day-before model and remain subject to the existing venue-outcome admission controls. Forecast rows expose `rainNowcast` even when a whole-day probability is unidentified.
+
 The existing `kalshi-weather-forecast` / `kalshi-weather-score` operations and `forecast-weather-markets-cli.mjs run|score|calibration` keep their configured NWS model, semantic journal, calibration and paper-sizing behavior. The general forecasting daily cycle continues to consume those records.
 
 The supplemental research and market collector: `node apps/weather.mjs cycle`, or the authenticated Cold Red Gate `weather_weather_cycle` tool. `weather_weather_status` shows coverage, gaps, scored model skill and available opportunities. `weather_weather_forecast` reads a specific contract. `weather_weather_model_admit` contributes a model experiment. `weather_weather_allocate` creates a depth-limited capital plan. These tools do not place orders; execution remains the custody-bound Kalshi desk.
@@ -75,3 +77,43 @@ The climate day uses local standard time. Missing hourly temperature/spread or u
 `weather_weather_relational_science` accepts `{"region":"nyc"}` or `{"region":"miami"}`. The equivalent command is `node apps/weather.mjs relational-science --region nyc`. It obtains a bounded 98-day IEM routine-METAR archive and tests next-report temperature increments using temporal and inter-station relations against persistence and a target-only control. All models fit and calibrate on earlier labels, and comparisons use identical cases. Raw reports, geometry, retrieval clocks and source hashes remain recoverable through `weather_weather_evidence`; contradictory reports remain explicit. This research does not register archive replays as forward forecast skill or trading admission.
 
 The [empirical science record](data/records/2026-10-07-relational-weather-metrology/README.md) gives the mathematical scope, measurements, reproducible results and limitations. This supplements operational NWS/NBM/LAMP forecasting and supports research without requiring any Kalshi market.
+
+## Learner-generating weather strategy research
+
+`weather_weather_strategy_research` with `{"region":"nyc"}` or `{"region":"miami"}` generates bounded relational learners, learns generators from earlier outcomes, and learns which generator to use. It evaluates exact predictive-mixture CRPS and explicitly hypothetical economic scenarios with adaptive rivals and conserved cash. The encoded arena is consumed and checked by the ecosystem's existing game runtime in the [scientific experiment](data/records/2026-10-07-weather-strategy-generators/README.md). Raw reports, frozen fits and full game plays are available through its content-addressed evidence ID. The CLI is `node apps/weather.mjs strategy-research --region nyc`. These retrospective studies preserve existing forecasting and trading admission; they do not send orders or claim real-market alpha.
+
+Prospective relational forecasts use the existing station-science consumer, retain empirical predictive laws and actual receipt/issuance clocks, and refuse expired or incomplete reporting windows. See [the implementation and observed checks](data/records/2026-10-07-prospective-relational-weather/README.md).
+
+## Operational ECMWF AI ensemble
+
+`weather_weather_ecmwf_evidence` retains the complete 51-member AIFS ENS v2 scenario array across requested stations and 1..4 future six-hour slots. Verified station geometry, all four projection corners, indexed GRIB2 bytes and real availability clocks stay recoverable through `weather_weather_evidence`; `rawFieldSha256` retrieves a matching retained field. The normal station collector adds this family when the private ecCodes decoder is installed. Physical forecast pools preserve its full empirical law and score it prospectively. See [the source, mathematical scope and hosted evidence](data/records/2026-10-07-ecmwf-joint-weather-ensemble/README.md). Six-hour projections have no daily-extreme or venue-admission claim.
+
+The existing city-index tools now push aligned AIFS members through certified city weights and offsets at exact six-hour slots, and preserve that empirical law in mixed pools. Certified PDF receipts define degraded-observation quorum; ambiguous half-cent ties retain probability bounds. [The joint-index science record](data/records/2026-10-07-joint-weather-index/README.md) retains six real prospective city forecasts and a sixty-probability snapshot against thirty live contracts. These are sensor proxies pending forward physical and exact venue validation.
+
+Forecast-family adaptation now runs within the existing physical station science. Each station or city, lead cohort, exact family composition, truth carrier and city configuration receives a separate past-only exponential-weight fit over paired daily CRPS differences. The fixed `paired-family-ewa-v1` protocol uses a 14-day rolling window, ten uniform prior days and a 10% uniform weight share. Multiple hours within a date change that date’s mean, rather than multiplying its learning weight. Full empirical atoms and Student-t components survive the weight transformation. Every adaptive forecast freezes its weights, fit clock, paired sufficient statistics and source digest, and carries the simultaneously issued equal pool as its comparator. The city-index contract consumer prices these frozen scientific laws only with matching configuration, composition, target and lead cohort. Physical index verification excludes fallback observations already known before forecast publication. This is a forward experiment: neither a CRPS improvement nor a synthetic regime-change result proves calibration, regret guarantees, opponent strategy identification or executable market alpha.
+
+Primary research informing this implementation: [Thorey, Mallet and Baudin, online CRPS learning](https://rmets.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/qj.2940), and [Zamo, Bel and Mestre, sequential aggregation and reliability](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.03540). The present fixed window, prior and uniform share are our experimental engineering choices; the papers’ guarantees are not claimed for this implementation. Reproducible mechanics and prospective receipts live in `data/records/2026-10-07-adaptive-weather-families/`.
+
+ECMWF transport fallback now uses its official regional S3, Google Cloud and direct ECMWF replicas after retryable HTTP failures. A field range is accepted only when that transport’s full index hash matches the selected immutable index. Receipts preserve both the requested logical URL and actual successful URL, failed transport clocks, byte range and index witness. The original cache identity and first receipt clock survive transport changes. Decoder metadata, full 51-member completeness, receipt-time checks and operating-reserve requirements still apply. A three-mirror real probe found byte-identical indexes and a 620,594-byte control temperature field. A separate controlled transport-failure experiment recovered and decoded that real field through Google Cloud, while rejecting mismatched indexes; it is not evidence that the source actually failed during that experiment. See `data/records/2026-10-07-ecmwf-transport-mirrors/`.
+
+Adaptive publications retain both their publication lead window (5–15, 15–30 or 30–60 minutes, otherwise the existing lead cohort) and frozen fit digest. A newly learned law can therefore be scored even when an earlier law for that target already exists. Metrics distinguish these lead windows; repeated fits for one target remain correlated forecast publications and do not add independent target dates. Each carries its equal-pool comparator from the same publication. Original physical and binary venue records remain available. Concurrent evidence collection reads the last atomic paired learning state without modifying the active writer’s lock or state; it preserves learned family weights and does not append outcomes from that read-only publication.
+
+
+Weather forecasting and weather-market participation have separate evaluations. Physical CRPS/calibration and exact-outcome Brier comparisons remain scientific evidence; outperforming a midpoint is not a universal prerequisite for useful quoting. The existing live admission controls still govern orders. A market participant also needs conditional fill-selection evidence, queue/latency measurements, inventory and capital control.
+
+`weather_participation` captures take/rest/wait alternatives for all available forecasted live weather contracts from frozen probabilities and fresh public books. Supply explicit scenario `capitalUsd`, optionally `encumberedUsd`, whole `contracts` and `windowSeconds` (5..300). Omit `tickers` for station-diverse discovery across all forecasted contracts; use optional `maxMarkets` (`--max-markets` in the CLI) for a smaller capture. Default discovery also binds newly listed hourly contracts from the already received city-index evidence, so listing discovery does not require another physical collection cycle. Current series fees and event overrides are retained; impending event fee changes shorten quote expiry. Metadata is fetched in batches and prepared before book requests containing at most 100 repeated `tickers` keys. Each batch preserves its actual receipt; no atomic exchange snapshot is claimed. Series and event fee observations are shared only inside this fresh capture, without a persistent fee cache. Coverage reports omitted or failed contracts. Monetary depth walks reuse the venue arena and upstream graded book calculations; exact rational average prices survive alongside numeric projections.
+
+Retrieve the returned `evidenceId` through `weather_evidence`. Pass it as `snapshotId` to review subsequent non-block public trades and exact, same-rule, final venue outcomes. Public trade pagination and an initial queue support only a conditional replay: absent order acknowledgments, changing price priority, publication delays and market impact prevent certification of a maker fill. Conditional maker probability and fill probability remain unknown. An empty or incomplete tape does not become demonstrated profitability. Reviews now expose `publicCounterpartyEvidence`: actual non-block public transactions in the captured receipt window, their opposite directional exposure, and purchase-equivalent gross payoffs when the consumer supplies an exact final label and certifies one-dollar binary face value. These are not actual counterparty strategy PnL: opening/closing positions, fees and member cash timing are unknown. Canonical outcome/book direction and legacy direction must agree. Conflicting identities, directions, clocks or quantities retain their witnesses and are excluded; a conflicted window cannot certify a complete queue replay. Public counterparties are a different selection population from our own absent orders, so our fill probability and conditional win law remain unknown.
+
+Pass `snapshotId` with `proposalActionIds` to verify an untrusted research proposal. The verifier checks scoped action identities, expiration, conflicts on each contract side and one cash budget across simultaneous YES/NO quotes. Unresolved fill-selection questions remain separately visible from competing commitments, following the game-foam double-banana distinction. This implements the proposer/verifier seam described in the Panini QMA-ready Reading specification; it makes no quantum-computing or profitability claim. The CLI exposes the same ability through `participation --capital 100 --contracts 3` or `participation --snapshot ID [--actions JSON_ARRAY]`, with `--full` for the retained record.
+
+The Cold Red Gate web handler and weather worker now resolve the same retained weather producer. Each retained release carries its actual entry in `manifest.json`; web calls resolve the current immutable release instead of importing weather code from an unrelated disposable house build. The normal local import remains available when no retained deployment exists. Public HTTP catalog activation must be verified separately from a fresh native MCP handler.
+
+The 2026-10-07 native host capture covered all 627 currently forecasted contracts (576 daily temperature, 30 hourly temperature and 21 rain) across 100 events and 34 locations. Seven metadata batches, 52 fresh series observations, 100 event observations and seven book batches replaced per-contract metadata/fee requests. An exploratory proposal of 959 one-contract resting bids reserved $618.46 of a hypothetical $1,000 budget; it is a feasibility demonstration, not an optimal policy. End-to-end capture took 74.15 seconds; proposal receipt followed the relevant books by 3.94–7.17 seconds. The pure verifier took 12.36 ms; native verification including archive loading and serialization took 997 ms. The snapshot retained 14.46 MB of JSON; the demonstration process reached 317.9 MiB peak RSS. These observations are in `data/records/2026-10-07-weather-participation/broad-capture-receipt.json` and `broad-verifier-profile.json`. Unforecasted listings, conditional maker selection and public HTTP catalog activation remain separate unfinished capabilities.
+
+Optional `quoteIntents` (`--quotes JSON` in the CLI) supplies scoped `{ticker, side, price, quantity?}` proposals, including initial bids on a side without displayed bids. Prices must lie on the observed price grid and stay strictly below the reciprocal offer. Legal lower bids may park cash behind better displayed bids. Initial quotes have no known queue ahead; changing priority and adverse selection remain unresolved. Below-best quotes retain the initial better-price and same-price queues. Their tape replay is explicitly blocked until a fuller book-event replay can account for price priority; quote formation and cash allocation remain available. These proposed prices are separate from physical forecast generation and confer no order authority.
+
+Pass `snapshotId` with `carryPolicy` (`--snapshot ID --carry JSON` in the CLI) to evaluate small carry bids against reserved cash and a holding hurdle. The policy requires `cases` containing `actionId`, conditional-on-full-fill `winProbabilityLow`/`winProbabilityHigh`, and `usableCashAtEarliest`/`usableCashAtLatest`. Optional `priorityReserveUsd` protects cash for better uses; `hourlyCashHurdle` is a dollar-per-dollar-per-hour opportunity cost; `minimumWinSurplusUsd` and `maxLossBudgetUsd` constrain selection. Captured resting actions are ranked greedily by conservative conditional net per dollar-hour; optimality and the conditional probability/cash-release assumptions remain unproved. The selected actions pass the existing shared-cash verifier using the residual budget. Allocation reads no venue data and does not refit weather models; its policy, evaluation and verifier result are retained through `weather_evidence`.
+
+A 97-cent bid does not imply a 97% conditional win probability. With a conservative one-cent fee reserve, winning returns two cents, but a 99% conditional win probability gives only one cent of expected net before opportunity cost. At 97% it gives minus one cent. On a fee-free cent-price contract the win surplus is three cents. Fee reserves now derive from the existing exact `scheduledFee` primitive: the venue rounds position cost plus fee to a centicent, and an integer-hundredth fragmentation bound replaces whole-cent rounding plus a blanket per-contract fragmentation overhead. The declared source patchset, precommitted cases, exact partition oracle, staged consumer receiving and failed first candidate are retained in `data/records/2026-10-07-weather-capital-opportunity`. Market close is not certified cash release; the scenario must supply that separate interval.
+
